---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_553",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 553,
  "text": "[[2544.14]] <b>434₂.  Principia theologiae eorum quos vulgo Quackeros vocant ex theologiae verae apologia Roberti Barclaii scoto-britanni\n[[2544.15]] EX THEOLOGIAE VERAE APOLOGIA ROBERTI BARCLAII\n[[2545.1]] <tit2><b>Principia Theologiae eorum quos vulgo Quackeros vocant ex Theologiae\n[[2545.2]] verae Apologia Roberti Barclaii Scoto-Britanni</tit2> </p>\n<p> [[2545.3]] 1) Summa hominis felicitas posita est in vera Dei cognitione. [thes. 1] </p>\n<p> [[2545.4]] 2) Deus recte cognosci non potest, nisi et cognitionis hujus fundamentum noscatur. [thes. 1,\n[[2545.5]] explic. cap. 1] </p>\n<p> [[2545.6]] 3) Formale fidei objectum est testimonium Spiritus internum. [thes. 2] </p>\n<p> [[2545.7]] 4) Scriptura sacra est velut rivus hujus fontis. Nam et ipsa nihil aliud est quam liber\n[[2545.8]] in quo consignata sunt ea quae Spiritus prophetis aut Apostolis dictavit. [thes. 3, explic.\n[[2545.9]] cap. 2] </p>\n<p> [[2545.10]] 5) Non creditur Scripturae vel Ecclesiae, vel traditioni nisi ob testimonium Spiritus\n[[2545.11]] internum. [thes. 3, explic. cap. 1] </p>\n<p> [[2545.12]] 6) Testimonium spiritus internum sibi ipsi criterium est sive ex eorum numero est,\n[[2545.13]] quae sunt per se clara, ut notiones communes v.g. <i>totum est majus parte</i>. [thes. 2] </p>\n<p> [[2545.14]] 7) Somnia, visiones, voces, literae, miracula non sunt formale fidei objectum, quia\n[[2545.15]] deceptioni diabolicae subjacent. [thes. 2, explic. cap. 8] </p>\n<p> [[2545.16]] 8) Testimonium spiritus internum nunquam pugnat Scripturae vel rationi. [thes. 2] </p>\n<p> [[2545.17]] 9) Per lapsum Adami in omnibus hominibus praevaluit semen quod Satanas\n[[2545.18]] sevit. [thes. 4] </p>\n<p> [[2545.19]] 10) Homo in statu corrupto sibi relictus nihil recte cognoscit agitque. [thes. 4] </p>\n<p> [[2545.20]] 11) Falsum est posse hominem in gratia Dei non constitutum, esse Evangelii ministrum\n[[2545.21]] et animabus prodesse. [thes. 4] </p>\n<p> [[2545.22]] 12) Nullum proprie loquendo est peccatum originis. [thes. 4, explic. cap. 4 f.] </p>\n<p> [[2545.23]] 13) Semen illud Satanae nemini imputatur nisi ei qui actu peccavit. [thes. 4] </p>\n<p> [[2545.24]] 14) Absurdum est infantes innocentes damnari. [thes. 4, explic. cap. 4] </p>\n<p> [[2545.25]] 15) Filius Dei ingenitus est lumen mentium. [thes. 5] </p>\n<p> [[2545.26]] 16) Lumen mentium hoc non minus universale est, quam semen peccati. [thes. 5] </p>\n<p> [[2545.27]] 17) Hoc lumen illuminavit omnem hominem venientem in hunc Mundum. [thes. 5-6] </p>\n<p> [[2545.29]] 18) Christus pro omnibus mortuus est cum effectu. [thes. 5-6, explic. cap. 6-8] </p>\n<p> [[2546.1]] 19) Nam Deus omnes constituit in actu proximo salutis, ita ut possint salvari si\n[[2546.2]] velint. [thes. 5-6, explic. cap. 11] </p>\n<p> [[2546.3]] 20) Non est necessaria ad salutem historia passionis Christi et externa Evangelii\n[[2546.4]] praedicatio: sufficit lumen mentium quod illuminat omnem hominem venientem in hunc\n[[2546.5]] mundum. [thes. 6] </p>\n<p> [[2546.6]] 21) In omnibus seculis et gentibus multi salvati sunt etiam ex antiquis philosophis;\n[[2546.7]] qui scilicet lumini mentium in se agenti non restiterunt, et spiritum Dei loquentem\n[[2546.8]] audiverunt. [thes. 6] </p>\n<p> [[2546.9]] 22) Lumen mentium docet: <i>quod tibi fieri nolis alteri non esse faciendum</i>, quod\n[[2546.10]] omnia includit, ipso Christo teste. [thes. 6] </p>\n<p> [[2546.11]] 23) Lumen mentium est caro Christi spiritualis, quam qui manducabunt non gustabunt\n[[2546.12]] mortem. [thes. 5-6, explic. cap. 13] </p>\n<p> [[2546.13]] 24) Lumen mentium non est habitus, sed substantia vera in nobis. Nam res denominantur\n[[2546.14]] ab accidentibus in se existentibus, v.g. <i>albus</i> ab albedine, non vero a substantiis,\n[[2546.15]] v.g. qui in se habet lapidem non dicitur <i>Saxeus</i>. Eodem modo etiam impius in se habet\n[[2546.16]] lumen mentium etsi ei resistat, nec ideo dicitur illuminatus. [thes. 5-6, explic. cap. 14] </p>\n<p> [[2546.17]] 25) Cognitio Christi secundum carnem, seu historia vitae mortisque ejus etsi non\n[[2546.18]] necessaria utilis tamen est, et ipso spiritus intus testificante, ab illis qui eam consequi\n[[2546.19]] possunt, non negligenda. Mirifice enim docet, atque excitat. [thes. 5-6, explic.\n[[2546.20]] cap. 15-16] </p>\n<p> [[2546.21]] 26) Conversi ac justificati et in gratia constituti sunt, qui pietatem justitiam caritatem,\n[[2546.22]] puritatem aliosque Spiritus S. fructus habent. [thes. 7] </p>\n<p> [[2546.23]] 27) Datur possibilitas non peccandi, fatendum est tamen facile esse labi nonnihil,\n[[2546.24]] etiam regeneratis quando non vigilantissime attendunt: ideo perfectio eorum recipit\n[[2546.25]] incrementum. [thes. 8] </p>\n<p> [[2546.26]] 28) Gratia amitti potest. [thes. 9] </p>\n<p> [[2546.27]] 29) Datur in hac vita gradus perfectionis a quo nulla contingere potest Apostasia. [thes. 9] </p>\n<p> [[2547.1]] 30) Omnis illuminatus sive in gratia constitutus est verus Evangelii minister, pastor,\n[[2547.2]] doctor, sacerdos; nec alia vocatione aut scientia indiget. [thes. 10] </p>\n<p> [[2547.3]] 31) Quisquis gratiae lumine caret ministerii ac sacerdotii est incapax quantamcunque\n[[2547.4]] demum habeat eruditionem aut autoritatem. [thes. 10] </p>\n<p> [[2547.5]] 32) Pastores donum Dei ut gratis accepere, ita gratis dare debent. Quicquid contra fit\n[[2547.6]] simonia est. [thes. 10] </p>\n<p> [[2547.7]] 33) Si quem Dominus avocaverit a negotio suo quo familiae panem comparare\n[[2547.8]] solitus est, ei permissum est ab aliis quae ad victum pertinent accipere, si ea ipsi <b>libere</b>\n[[2547.9]] dentur. [thes. 10] </p>\n<p> [[2547.10]] 34) Verus Dei cultus nec locis, nec temporibus nec personis praescriptis limitatur. [thes. 11] </p>\n<p> [[2547.12]] 35) Omnes preces caeremoniales, quibus certum tempus locusque praescribitur et\n[[2547.13]] omnis cultus pro humana commoditate constitutus, est <greek>ĕuelourhskeía</greek> et idololatria\n[[2547.14]] abominabilis in conspectu Dei. Sequendus est enim impulsus Spiritus S. [thes. 11] </p>\n<p> [[2547.15]] 36) Unum est tantum Baptisma, scilicet Spiritus S. et ignis. Baptisma infantum est\n[[2547.16]] mera traditio humana. [thes. 12] </p>\n<p> [[2547.17]] 37) Fractio panis per Christum cum discipulis erat figura spiritualis communionis\n[[2547.18]] cum carne Christi, qua homo interior nutritur. Quae autem intelligatur caro Christi supra\n[[2547.19]] dictum est n. 23. [thes. 13] </p>\n<p> [[2547.20]] 38) Fractio panis non magis necessaria est, quam abstinere a sanguine et suffocato,\n[[2547.21]] lavare invicem pedes, infirmos oleo ungere: talia cum sint tantum umbrae meliorum illis\n[[2547.22]] non sunt necessaria, qui substantiam assecuti sunt. [thes. 13] </p>\n<p> [[2547.23]] 39) Solus Deus conscientiarum est Dominus. Caedes, carceres, exilia, proscriptiones\n[[2547.24]] dissentientium, semper injustae. [thes. 14] </p>\n<p> [[2547.25]] 40) Nemini licet praetextu impellentis conscientiae turbas movere vel cuiquam\n[[2547.26]] nocere; qui secus faciet juste punietur. [thes. 14] </p>\n<p> [[2547.27]] 41) Detectio capitis, flexio corporis caeteraeque stultae et superstitiosae formalitates\n[[2547.28]] non faciunt nisi ad fovendam humanam superbiam ideoque negligi debent. [thes. 15] </p>\n<p> [[2547.29]] 42) Ludi inutiles frivolaeque nugae quas vocant recreationes non nisi ad pretiosum\n[[2547.30]] tempus perdendum inventae sunt, mentemque ab audiendo spiritu intus loquente, et sensu\n[[2548.1]] vivace timoris Dei divertunt, ideoque a vero Christiano damnari et vitari\n[[2548.2]] debent. [thes. 15] </p>\n",
  "number": "434₂.",
  "title": "Principia theologiae eorum quos vulgo Quackeros vocant ex theologiae verae apologia Roberti Barclaii scoto-britanni",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:434₂. Principia theologiae eorum quos vulgo Quackeros vocant ex theologiae verae apologia Roberti Barclaii scoto-britanni EX THEOLOGIAE VERAE APOLOGIA ROBERTI BARCLAII Principia Theologiae eorum quos vulgo Quackeros vocant ex Theologiae verae Apologia Roberti Barclaii Scoto-Britanni 1) Summa hominis...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>